Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis An alternative to overloading operator[] is using an at() function. string& at(int index) { if (index < 0 || index >= static_cast(tracks.size())) { throw out_of_range("Invalid index"); }

return tracks[index]; }

Operation Time complexity Extra space Prefix increment O(1) O(1) Postfix increment O(1) O(1) Comparison operators O(1) O(1) Checked operator[] O(1) O(1) at() function O(1) O(1) Unchecked array access O(1) O(1)

Checked access performs an additional comparison before returning the element. All approaches have O(1) time complexity, but checked access provides better protection against invalid indexes. 9. Conclusion The program successfully demonstrates operator overloading using prefix and postfix increment, comparison operators and the subscript operator. Prefix increment is generally preferred for class objects because it avoids creating an unnecessary temporary copy. Range checking also improves program safety by preventing invalid playlist access.
